Mark externally stored ezm7 tensors as external data.

ezm7EncodeWithExternalStore writes the payload to the external store but
doesn't set 0x1000_0000 in the identifier (unlike other external encoders).

Readers attempting to decode it will return zeros, or garbage, or possibly
even crash due to out-of-bounds memory access.  If you then recompact the
store with TensorData.makeCompactStore, the row is skipped and lost forever.
